/b></div><b>About Molecular Connections&#10;</b><div>Molecular Connections is a leading AI/ML driven data science and content solutions company partnering with global leaders in scholarly publishing, STEM, and pharma.&#10;</div><div><b><br></b></div><div>Headquartered in Bengaluru with multiple delivery centres across South India, the company has over two decades of experience in structuring scientific information using proprietary AI models and knowledge graphs.</div><div><br></div><div><b>What You Will Do</b><div><br><div></div><div>Transform experimental chemistry data from journals and patents into structured, searchable knowledge powering our chemistry intelligence platforms.&#10;</div><div><br></div><div>Extract, interpret, and curate reactions, substances, and property data, and annotate them using internal curation tools and cheminformatics systems (e.g., SMILES, InChI, structure editors).&#10;</div><div><br></div><div>Ensure accuracy, consistency, and standardization of data across multiple sources to build high quality chemistry databases used by scientists worldwide.&#10;</div><div><br></div><div>Stay updated on evolving chemical databases, data standards, and digital chemistry trends, while collaborating with cross functional experts in data science and product.&#10;</div><div><br></div><div><b>Who Should Apply</b></div><div><br></div><div>Master&#8217;s degree (or Integrated M.Sc.) in Chemistry, Pharmaceutical Sciences, Chemical Engineering, or closely related fields from NITs, IISERs, IITs, and other tier 1 institutes.&#10;</div><div><br></div><div>Strong understanding of organic and inorganic chemistry, reaction mechanisms, and physicochemical/biological properties of compounds, with the ability to interpret primary literature and patents.&#10;</div><div><br></div><div>Added advantages (not mandatory): Familiarity with cheminformatics concepts/tools (SMILES, InChI, structure editors), basic coding/scripting, or exposure to chemical databases.&#10;</di